course: dictionary
lesson: 3890
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Many words have more than one meaning, and the sentence tells you which one to use. The word fresh is a good example. «Fresh bread» means bread that was made recently, not old or stale.
explain: The same word can also mean something clean and cool. «Open the window for fresh air» means cool, clean air, not new air. Ask yourself which meaning fits the sentence best.
explain: Fresh can also mean a new beginning. «Peter was given a fresh start» means he got another chance to begin again. Test each meaning by putting it into the sentence and checking that it still makes sense.
fact: Fresh is an adjective here: it describes a noun such as bread, air or water.
fact: «Fresh» can mean recently made or picked, as in «fresh fruit».
fact: «Fresh» can mean clean and cool, as in «fresh air».
fact: Fresh water, from rivers and lakes, is not salty; most of Earth's water is salty sea water.
fact: «A fresh start» means a new beginning.
exercise: «The bakery sells fresh bread every morning.» What does fresh mean here? | Painted in bright colours | *Recently made, not old | Used before | Cold and wet
exercise: «Ben opened the window to let in some fresh air.» What does fresh mean here? | Very loud | Warm and stuffy | Full of smoke | *Clean and cool
exercise: «Fish that live in rivers and lakes are called freshwater fish.» Is the water they live in fresh or salty? | *Fresh, not salty | Frozen all year | Salty, like the sea | Hot, like soup
test: «After the storm, the air felt fresh and cool.» What does fresh mean? | Very loud | *Clean and cool | Hot and dusty
test: «Sam wanted a fresh start at his new school.» What does fresh mean? | *A new beginning | Covered in mud | Dirty | Old and worn
exam: «After a good night's sleep, Mia felt fresh and full of energy.» What does fresh mean? | Tired and sleepy | Dirty and cold | Wet from rain | *Rested and full of energy
